---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Tien Nguyen — AI-native PM/PO. Career: Green SM platform ops, Colonial insurtech delivery, Hoookie/Olmo. Public demos: Knowledge Engine, Recon, Sport Quant, Gelato."
>
  <section class="page-head section">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Career panorama — what ships on the resume vs what you can click.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      AI-native Product Manager / Product Owner (she/her), ex-full-stack engineer, Ho Chi Minh City.
      The PDF resume is being refreshed; this page is the live map of employment vs inspectable
      demos.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Now</p>
      <h2>Green SM / GSM (Vingroup) — platform ops.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        Day job: platform operations that connect Green SM ecosystems — food, driver, and related
        surfaces under the Vingroup mobility company (
        <a href="https://www.greensm.com/vn-vi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >greensm.com</a
        >). Timeline and title belong on the resume. Architecture and internals stay confidential —
        not published as case studies or demos.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-label="Career ledger">
    <div class="about-ledger">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Employers (no public demo)</h3>
        <p>
          Green SM / GSM (Vingroup) — current platform ops across ecosystems. Colonial Surety —
          prior insurtech / B2B fintech PME (PCI cutover, bundling, SSO, PM controls) — resume
          facts only. Hoookie (Keeta, Sire.bot), Olmo (+30% bookings), 4/10 ERP path.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Demo use cases (open these)</h3>
        <p>
          Knowledge Engine, Sport Quant, Recon — live today. Gelato agentic platform suite
          (control plane + six verticals) — brief now; full demos when builds are real.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Also building</h3>
        <p>
          Petmood (pet triage beta, HCMC), AnDigi (agent-operated insurance, in design), Vietnam
          fashion-retail SME advisory (forward-deployed).
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid about-closing">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Interview hook</p>
      <h2>Lead with inspectable systems. Prove delivery on the resume.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        HR and interviewers should open Knowledge Engine first (source-traced specs + human
        sign-off), then Sport Quant (deterministic gates), then Recon. Employer depth (Green SM,
        Colonial) stays conversational + resume — never a leaked platform tour.
      </p>
      <div class="action-row">
        <a class="button" href={withBase('/works/')}>Case studies</a>
        <a class="text-link" href={withBase('/Tien-Nguyen-CV.pdf')}>Resume PDF (being updated)</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
